**Usage example**
```tsx
<CheckoutScreen
  items={cartItems}
  currency="USD"
  deliveryFee={4.99}
  onBack={() => navigate('/cart')}
  onPay={async (address) => {
    await api.createOrder({ items: cartItems, address });
    navigate('/order-confirmation');
  }}
/>
```

Notes:
- Styling uses `var(--tg-theme-*)` CSS variables so it inherits the user's actual Telegram theme (light/dark), with sane fallbacks for browser preview.
- `BackButton` integration is optional/defensive — it no-ops outside Telegram, and the in-page back arrow works everywhere.
- Validation runs on submit and per-field on blur; the Pay button stays enabled (rather than disabled) so a tap surfaces which fields need fixing, matching common Mini App UX.
